oducing, and using enterprise data that is at issue in legal matters. It also provides DISCO Review, an AI-powered document review that delivers legal document reviews; and DISCO Case Builder that allows legal professionals to collaborate across teams by offering a single place to search, organize, and review witness testimony and other important legal data. The company's products are used for various legal matters comprising litigation, investigation, compliance, and diligence. It serves enterprises, law firms, legal services providers, and governments. CS Disco, Inc. was founded in 2012 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eric  Friedrichsen | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 577 people. Revenue per employee of $272K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $42K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["CS Disco, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $387M market cap on $157M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -209% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 75% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $18M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 16% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 23% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 37% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (75% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.25},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 156% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"CS Disco (NYSE:LAW) Stock: Insider Melanie Antoon Sells 9,036 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/cs-disco-nyselaw-stock-insider-melanie-antoon-sells-9036-shares.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795172928.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CS 